# Generated coverage reports. `apps/api/coverage/` is istanbul/nyc output (clover.xml,
# an empty coverage-final.json, prettify.js) — i.e. a JS coverage reporter writing into
# the GO app's directory, which is its own bug (see disc-2026-09-js-coverage-in-apps-api).
# Ignoring it here stops it breaking `format:check`; it is deliberately NOT in .gitignore,
# because that would change what git picks up rather than what prettier reads.
apps/api/coverage/

# TestSprite run reports are generated HTML. They ARE committed on purpose (see
# `git log -- 'testsprite_tests/*.html'`), so they belong here, not in .gitignore —
# there is even a `chore(testsprite): prettier-format generated HTML report` commit
# in the history showing what happens when they are not ignored.
testsprite_tests/*.html
